## 5. Autentikasi & Session (NextAuth v5)

### 5.1 Arsitektur Auth

Sistem auth dibagi menjadi 2 file untuk optimasi:

#### `auth.config.ts` (Edge-Safe)

```typescript
// TIDAK import Prisma atau bcrypt — bisa di-import di edge/proxy
export const authConfig = {
  pages: { signIn: "/login" },
  session: {
    strategy: "jwt",
    maxAge: 60 * 60 * 8,  // 8 jam
  },
  providers: [],  // Ditambahkan di auth.ts
  callbacks: {
    jwt({ token, user }) {
      // Persist id + role ke JWT token saat sign-in
      if (user) {
        token.id = user.id
        token.role = user.role ?? "AUTHOR"
      }
      return token
    },
    session({ session, token }) {
      // Expose id + role di session object
      session.user.id = token.id
      session.user.role = token.role ?? "AUTHOR"
      return session
    },
  },
}
```

#### `auth.ts` (Server-Side Only)

```typescript
// Import Prisma + bcrypt (berat, hanya untuk auth handler)
export const { handlers, auth, signIn, signOut } = NextAuth({
  ...authConfig,
  providers: [
    Credentials({
      credentials: { email: {...}, password: {...} },
      async authorize(rawCredentials, request) {
        // 1. Validate input via Zod (email: lowercase, trimmed)
        // 2. Rate limit check: 5 attempts / 15 minutes per IP+email
        // 3. Query user by email
        // 4. TIMING-SAFE compare: selalu bcrypt.compare, bahkan jika user tidak ada
        //    (gunakan DUMMY_PASSWORD_HASH untuk prevent enumeration)
        // 5. Jika match → return { id, email, name, role }
        // 6. Jika gagal → consumeLoginAttempt() + return null
        // 7. NEVER return passwordHash ke session layer
      },
    }),
  ],
})
```

**Anti-patterns yang dihindari**:

- Timing side channel → dummy hash comparison
- User enumeration → generic error message
- Brute force → rate limit per IP+email (5/15min)
- Password in session → explicit field exclusion

### 5.2 Proxy / Middleware (`proxy.ts`)

```typescript
// Edge middleware — runs on EVERY matched request
export const proxy = auth((req) => {
  // Logic:
  // 1. /admin/* atau /api/admin/* + NOT logged in → redirect ke /login?redirect=path
  // 2. /login + logged in → redirect ke /admin
  // 3. Otherwise → NextResponse.next()
})

export const config = {
  matcher: ["/admin/:path*", "/api/admin/:path*", "/login"],
}
```

**PENTING**: Proxy hanya cek "apakah ada session?" — BUKAN cek role. Role authorization di-enforce di `requireAdminPage()` dan `requireAdminApi()` (defense in depth).

### 5.3 Login Page Flow

```text
User buka /admin
  → proxy.ts: belum login → redirect /login?redirect=/admin
  → Login page renders (client component)
  → User submit email + password
  → signIn("credentials", { email, password, redirect: false })
  → auth.ts authorize() runs:
      → Zod validate
      → Rate limit check
      → DB lookup + bcrypt compare
      → Return user atau null
  → Jika sukses → router.push(redirect) + router.refresh()
  → Jika gagal → tampilkan "Email atau password salah"
```

