## 10. API Routes — Detail per Endpoint

### 10.1 Posts API

#### `GET /api/admin/posts`

- Auth: `requireAdminApi()`
- Query: `{ page, limit, status?, search?, category? }`
- Validation: Zod schema
- Response: `{ success, data: Post[], pagination: { page, limit, total, totalPages } }`

#### `POST /api/admin/posts`

- Auth: `requireAdminMutationApi()` (includes CSRF + rate limit)
- Body: `{ title, slug, content?, excerpt?, featuredImage?, status?, publishedAt?, scheduledAt?, categoryIds?, tagIds?, metaTitle?, metaDescription?, ... }`
- Logic:
  1. Zod validate body
  2. Parse dates (publishedAt, scheduledAt)
  3. Check slug uniqueness
  4. Sanitize HTML content
  5. If PUBLISHED: validate readiness (title ≥10 chars, content ≥120 words, excerpt required)
  6. If SCHEDULED: require scheduledAt
  7. Calculate reading time
  8. Create post with categories + tags relations
  9. If published: revalidatePath
  10. Log admin action
- Response: `{ success, data: Post }`

#### `GET /api/admin/posts/[id]`

- Returns single post with all fields + categories + tags

#### `PUT /api/admin/posts/[id]`

- Same validation as POST but for update
- Handles category/tag reassignment (delete old → create new)

#### `DELETE /api/admin/posts/[id]`

- Cascade deletes: CategoriesOnPosts, TagsOnPosts
- revalidatePath

### 10.2 Categories API

#### `GET /api/admin/categories`

```json
{ "success": true, "data": [{ "id": "1", "name": "Category", "slug": "cat", "description": null, "_count": { "posts": 5 } }] }
