## 14. Scheduled Publishing (Cron)

### Publisher Logic (`lib/content/scheduled-publisher.ts`)

```typescript
// Called by cron endpoint: POST /api/admin/posts/publish-scheduled
// or GET /api/cron/publish-scheduled (with cron secret)

export async function publishDueScheduledPosts(now: Date) {
  // 1. Query: status=SCHEDULED, scheduledAt <= now, LIMIT 50, ORDER BY scheduledAt ASC
  // 2. For each post:
  //    a. validatePublishReadiness() — same rules as manual publish
  //    b. If fails: push scheduledAt 1 hour ahead (backoff), add to skipped
  //    c. If passes: CAS update (WHERE id AND status=SCHEDULED) → PUBLISHED
  //    d. Update linked ContentIdea status to "published"
  //    e. Add to published list
  // 3. Return { checked, published, skipped }
}
```

**CAS (Compare-And-Swap)**: `updateMany({ where: { id, status: "SCHEDULED" } })` ensures two concurrent cron runs can't both publish the same post.

### Publish Validation Rules

```typescript
// lib/content/post-publishing.ts
function validatePublishReadiness(input) {
  const issues = []
  if (title.length < 10) issues.push("Judul minimal 10 karakter")
  if (wordCount < 120) issues.push("Konten minimal 120 kata")
  if (!excerpt && !metaDescription) issues.push("Excerpt/metaDescription wajib")
  return issues
}
```

