## 18. Data Migration Guide (Payload CMS → Sistem Ini)

### 18.1 Data Mapping

| Payload CMS Collection | Target Model | Migration Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Users | User | Map roles, hash passwords |
| Posts | Post | Map content, SEO fields, categories, tags |
| Categories | Category | Preserve slugs |
| Tags | Tag | Preserve slugs |
| Pages | Page | Map content + SEO |
| Media | Media | Transfer URLs, preserve alt text |
| Settings (global) | SiteSetting | Map to key-value pairs |

### 18.2 Migration Script Strategy

```typescript
// scripts/migrate-from-payload.ts

async function migrateFromPayload() {
  // 1. Connect to Payload CMS database (source)
  // 2. Connect to target PostgreSQL (Prisma)
  
  // 3. Migrate Users
  // - Map Payload user fields → User model
  // - Hash passwords if needed
  // - Set role: ADMIN for admin users
  
  // 4. Migrate Categories
  // - Preserve name, slug
  // - Generate cuid() IDs
  // - Track old_id → new_id mapping
  
  // 5. Migrate Tags
  // - Same pattern as categories
  
  // 6. Migrate Media
  // - Transfer Cloudinary URLs or re-upload
  // - Preserve alt, width, height
  
  // 7. Migrate Posts
  // - Map content (HTML), title, slug
  // - Map SEO fields
  // - Link categories via CategoriesOnPosts (use ID mapping)
  // - Link tags via TagsOnPosts
  // - Preserve publishedAt dates
  // - Set source: "migrated"
  
  // 8. Migrate Pages
  // - Same as posts but simpler
  
  // 9. Migrate Settings
  // - Map Payload globals → SiteSetting records
  
  // 10. Verify counts match
  // 11. Verify slug uniqueness
  // 12. Verify relation integrity
}
```

### 18.3 Critical Migration Rules

1. **NEVER lose data**: Every field must have a target
2. **Preserve URLs**: All slugs must match exactly (for SEO)
3. **Preserve dates**: publishedAt, createdAt must be exact
4. **Preserve relations**: Post ↔ Category/Tag mappings
5. **Preserve media URLs**: If using same Cloudinary, URLs stay the same
6. **Redirect legacy routes**: next.config.ts handles /blog/:slug → /:slug
7. **Preserve SEO**: meta titles, descriptions, canonical URLs

