## 19. Workflow Lengkap — End to End

### 19.1 User Login Flow

```text
1. User navigates to /admin
2. proxy.ts checks: no session → redirect /login?redirect=/admin
3. Login page renders (client component)
4. User enters email + password
5. signIn("credentials", { email, password, redirect: false })
6. Server: Zod validate → rate limit check → DB lookup → bcrypt compare
7. Success: JWT token created with { id, role }
8. Client: router.push("/admin") + router.refresh()
9. Admin layout: requireAdminPage() verifies role
10. Dashboard renders with stats
```

### 19.2 Create Post Flow

```text
1. User clicks "Tulis Artikel" → /admin/posts/new
2. PostEditor component renders (empty state)
3. User types title → auto-generate slug
4. User writes content in TipTap editor
5. User selects categories, tags
6. User uploads/selects featured image
7. User fills SEO metadata (or uses AI suggestions)
8. User clicks "Publish" or "Save Draft"
9. Client:
   a. Validate required fields client-side
   b. Get CSRF token (if not cached)
   c. POST /api/admin/posts with all data
10. Server:
   a. requireAdminMutationApi() → auth + CSRF + rate limit
   b. Zod validate body
   c. Check slug uniqueness
   d. Sanitize HTML content
   e. If PUBLISHED: validatePublishReadiness()
   f. Calculate reading time
   g. Prisma create with nested category/tag relations
   h. If published: revalidatePath
   i. Log admin action
11. Client: redirect to post list or show success
```

### 19.3 Scheduled Publish Flow

```text
1. User sets status = SCHEDULED, picks future date
2. Post saved with status=SCHEDULED, scheduledAt=<future>
3. Cron job runs periodically (e.g. every 5 minutes)
4. Calls publishDueScheduledPosts()
5. Finds posts where scheduledAt <= now
6. For each: validatePublishReadiness()
7. If passes: CAS update SCHEDULED → PUBLISHED
8. If fails: push scheduledAt 1 hour ahead
9. Linked ContentIdea updated to "published"
```

### 19.4 AI Content Generation Flow

```text
1. User goes to /admin/ai/generate
2. Enters topic, keywords, target length
3. Client: POST /api/admin/ai/generate
4. Server:
   a. Fetch AiRoleModel where role="text"
   b. Build prompt with topic + keywords + site context
   c. Call AI provider (Gemini or OpenAI-compatible)
   d. Parse generated content
   e. Create AiTask record for tracking
5. Return generated content to editor
6. User reviews, edits, then saves as post
```

### 19.5 Content Audit Flow

```text
1. Admin triggers content audit
2. Server fetches all published posts
3. AI "scanning" model analyzes:
   - Content coverage gaps
   - Missing internal links
   - SEO improvement opportunities
4. Creates ContentIdea records (30-day calendar)
5. Creates InternalLinkSuggestion records
6. Results displayed in /admin/ai/content-audit
7. Admin can:
   - Schedule ideas to calendar
   - Convert ideas to draft posts
   - Apply internal link suggestions (auto-edit HTML)
   - Dismiss suggestions
```

